### Topic 30 - Logging in Spring Boot
### Start the app first: mvn spring-boot:run
### After each request, look at the console and at logs/food-delivery.log

### 1. Place an order -> DEBUG + INFO logs (card number is masked!)
POST http://localhost:8080/orders?customer=Asha&item=Pizza&quantity=2

### 2. Place an order with OUR OWN request id -> see [req:my-id-123] in the logs
POST http://localhost:8080/orders?customer=Ravi&item=Biryani&quantity=1
X-Request-Id: my-id-123

### 3. Invalid quantity -> WARN log and 400 Bad Request
POST http://localhost:8080/orders?customer=Asha&item=Pizza&quantity=99

### 4. Find an order (ids start at 1001)
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/1001

### 5. Unknown order -> WARN log and 404
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/9999

### 6. Simulated failure -> ERROR log WITH stack trace
POST http://localhost:8080/orders/1001/notify

### 7. One message at every level
GET http://localhost:8080/orders/levels-demo
